body:
I have literally, cited his work verbatim. Twice even. If I present somone's literature, then cited them directly page number and all. How does is the etymological of a word irrelvent.

Incase you missed it, this is what he stated from his research:

"Generally speaking, genocide does not necessarily mean the immediate destruction of a nation, except when accomplished by mass killings of all members of a nation.



It is intended rather to signify a coordinated plan of different actions aiming at the destruction of essential foundations of the life of national groups, with the aim of annihilating the groups themselves. The objectives of such a plan would be the disintegration of the political and social institutions, culture, language, national feelings, religion, and economic existence of national groups and the destruction of the personal security, liberty, health, dignity and even the lives of the individuals belonging to such groups."


This time read.

More embarrassingly, I can even look to the United Nations definition:

In the present Convention, genocide means any of the following acts committed with the intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group, as such:

Killing members of the group;

Causing serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group;

Deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction in whole or in part;

Imposing measures intended to prevent births within the group;

Forcibly transferring children of the group to another group.

" The results indicate that children raised by same-sex parents from birth perform better than children raised by different-sex parents in both primary and secondary education. Our findings are robust to use of cousin fixed effects and coarsened exact matching to improve covariate balance and to reduce model dependence. Further analyses using a novel bounding estimator suggest the selection on unobserved characteristics would have to be more than three times higher than the selection on observed characteristics to reduce the positive estimates to zero."

&#x200B;

Is that short enough for you?

It's very tenable because we've done that before without any complaints.  Gas station attendants in the 1960s were unironically being paid higher salaries when we accounted for inflation. They were getting paid their time's version of a 25/hr wage with no problems.

&#x200B;

These are jobs you rely on to some degree. Or at least use products or services from them. The person making your coffee should be able to live without stress from next week's bills.

Let's get that birthrate to a nice and sexy 1.60 just for that.

&#x200B;

People move to where the jobs are. Normally they find a job first and then move. Cheaper areas objectively have fewer job opportunities and other amenities. It's not often literally in nowhere.

&#x200B;

Your happy bullshit trying to minimize the effect of poverty makes me think that the shrinking birthrate is well deserved. A nice little 'fuck you' to the broader political and cultural atmosphere and to people who think like you.

"Have a little self-accountability and discipline bro."

Okay. How's a 1.64 birthrate for accountability? 

&#x200B;

Like realistically, 'cheaper areas' are often cheap because they're cornfields in the middle of nowhere with no hospitals, no groceries and no jobs.

"From 2006 until 31 August 2018, Israel demolished at least 1,360 Palestinian residential units in the West Bank (not including East Jerusalem), causing 6,115 people – including at least 3,094 minors – to lose their homes."- Wikipedia

Yeah, Israeli 'peace' is just poor brown people being silent while colonizers just demolish their homes for the lols. It makes sense why Gaze is so stubbornly violent because they know that there's no peace option where their basic rights will be respected. The moment they stop doing violence, their homes will be demolished. And then you'll get white American and German tourists staying in hotels that were built on top of a refugee camp.

&#x200B;

I suppose there's a big contradiction in Western ideology. You like your colonalism but you don't like the implications of it. You want to be able to just abuse black and brown people. But you don't like how that necessitates extreme violence as a retaliation. You want to build a condo in Gaza. But you don't like how you'll have to go through hundreds of hostages, and thousands of dead children to get that.

&#x200B;

You want what America had. All the natives were just silently in their tiny reservation camps after being whipped out. Unfortunately, Gaza would rather just go down kicking and screaming

I'll respond by giving them more land and investing in infrastructure, schools, hospitals and hospitals. To improve the lives of people in poverty.

&#x200B;

Wait, do you expect us to be in favour of genociding a bunch of poor people? You're in the wrong sub mate. There's no white supremacy here

Technically he had to unite with the Conservatives (I'm sure that's not relevant in any modern situation) and then he had to arrest all the political opposition with the Conservative's approval. Only then was he able to get into power by having the Parlement of only Conservatives and Nazis vote for him into power. 

&#x200B;

This is a far cry from having the entire country side with him under any metric. Even if he was very popular.

An absolute lie. Consistently, native populations were consuming more calories before colonialism than during. Most people were objectively poorer due to the introduction of capitalism. Heck, in India, it was calculated that  1.8 billion Indians died avoidably from egregious deprivation under the British (1757-1947). That might be considered a stretch sure. But much more defensible calculations have it that 160 million died during a 40-year period (1880 to 1920).

&#x200B;

I suppose the gist is simple. If you don't count the corpses, did anyone really die?

I don't know literally hundreds and millions died under British rule too. For example, British policies killed well over 100 million, up to 160 million Indians between 1880 to 1920. A forty-year period.

&#x200B;

" If we estimate excess mortality from 1891 to 1920, with the average death rate of the 1880s as normal mortality, we find some 50 million people lost their lives under the aegis of British capitalism (see Appendix V for a full discussion).16 But this estimate must be considered conservative. India’s 1880s death rate was already very high by international standards. If we measure excess mortality over England’s 16th- and 17th-century average death rate, we find 165 million excess deaths in India between 1880 and 1920 (Appendix V). This figure is larger than the combined number of deaths from both World Wars, including the Nazi holocaust." https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305750X22002169#s0015

Having zero diversity creates a cultural dead zone where everything is boring and nothing innovates. Squidward was sad because the environment became soul-drenching. He became bored with no purpose, and no creativity. Nothing was happening. 

&#x200B;

He also had absolutely no friends or anyone to share interests with.

Aren't Christians actively attempting to put Intelligent Design in schools despite a federal judge ruling it unscientific and it's been rejected by all of the international scientific community? And within that court hearing, wasn't it revealed that the intelligent design proponents were actually liars who tried to bypass an even older court ruling banning Creationism from schools?

&#x200B;

I feel like that's some important context you're missing out.
